course: dictionary
lesson: 772
title: Bearded: a word for hair and for creatures
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday.» Here bearded is part of a creature's name, so it is not about a face at all.
explain: Bearded first means having a beard, the hair that grows on the chin and cheeks. «A bearded man» helps you picture him. Writers use describing words like bearded so the reader can see a character clearly.
explain: In animals and plants, bearded means having tufts of hair or bristles. The bearded vulture is a large bird, and bearded capuchins are monkeys, so the word names a feature, not a person. Ask yourself what the word is describing: a person, an animal or a plant?
fact: Bearded means having a beard, hair growing on the chin and cheeks.
fact: In animals and plants, bearded describes tufts of hair or bristles.
fact: A bearded dragon is a lizard from the dry lands of Australia, and it is a popular pet.
fact: The bearded vulture is a large bird that eats mostly bones.
fact: Bearded is a describing word, so it tells you more about a noun such as a man, a dragon or a monkey.
exercise: «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday.» In this sentence, what is a bearded dragon? | A large bird that eats bones | *A lizard from Australia that is a popular pet | A man with a long grey beard | A plant with tufts of hair
exercise: «The bearded vulture eats mostly bones and drops big ones onto rocks from high up to crack them.» What kind of creature is the bearded vulture? | *A large bird | A monkey from Brazil | A lizard from the desert | A small fish
exercise: «The bearded man smiled and waved at the children.» What does bearded tell you about the man? | He is a monkey from Brazil | He is sleeping under a tree | *He has hair growing on his chin and cheeks | He is a bird with tufts of feathers
test: «Bearded capuchins in Brazil crack hard palm nuts on a flat rock.» Where do bearded capuchins live? | Australia | Scotland | *Brazil | Arizona
test: «A bearded dragon bobbing its head is signalling that it is in charge.» What does the head bobbing show? | *That it is in charge | Crying | Hiding in the sand | Eating a bone
exam: In «the bearded vulture», what does bearded describe? | The colour of its wings | A beard on a person's chin | *Tufts of hair or bristles on the bird | The place where it lives
